{
  "date": "20261004",
  "method": "Each suite runs in a fresh container of the distribution, with only that distribution's packages for the linked X11/OpenGL/font libraries plus Xvfb; smoke-runner runs on a real X display (xcb for Qt 6). Baseline rows use the suite's own floor distribution.",
  "evidence": "artifacts/runtime-linux-forward/20261004",
  "conclusions": [
    "qt4-sarge-i386 (built 2026-10-02) passes 24/24 applications and 525 checks with no failure on Ubuntu 16.04, 18.04, 24.04, Debian 13 and Fedora 44 with 32-bit libraries installed; Arch has no 32-bit libraries by default and is not tested.",
    "qt4-ubuntu16-amd64 is a stale 2026-08-15 build (commit 429f22e). Its widgets-gallery crashes identically on its own Ubuntu 16.04 and on every newer distribution, so this is not a forward regression; the set must be rebuilt from the current tree.",
    "qt6-ubuntu18-amd64 is built without fontconfig and finds no fonts unless QT_QPA_FONTDIR is set; without it font/metrics fails everywhere, including Ubuntu 18.04.",
    "qt6-ubuntu18-amd64 widgets-gallery and quick-qml-gallery crash under xcb on Xvfb on Ubuntu 18.04 as well; the earlier Bionic proof used the offscreen platform. Not a forward regression, but an open X11 issue.",
    "Forward regression: on Ubuntu 24.04, Debian 13, Fedora 44 and Arch, qt6-ubuntu18-amd64 has no TLS (QSslSocket::supportsSsl() is false). The build loads OpenSSL 1.1 at run time and these distributions ship only OpenSSL 3; net/tls-loopback-handshake and network/dtls-value-types fail."
  ],
